1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:04,296
Are you thinkin' about taking drugs?

2
00:00:04,370 --> 00:00:08,309
Well, think again,
because drugs are not the answer.

3
00:00:08,377 --> 00:00:10,369
Take it from me, Hank Wiggen.

4
00:00:11,516 --> 00:00:13,610
Oh, don't remember this ugly mug?

5
00:00:15,289 --> 00:00:19,228
Two years ago, I was a star.
I won n-nine games in a row.

6
00:00:19,296 --> 00:00:22,927
- But by the end of August, I was gone-
- Cut! Cut!

7
00:00:26,978 --> 00:00:29,847
- Not good, huh?
- Well, you caught the ball.

8
00:00:29,916 --> 00:00:31,475
Yeah.

9
00:00:31,552 --> 00:00:37,256
Look, I usually don't, you know,
give line readings, but let me-Try this.

10
00:00:37,329 --> 00:00:39,298
Hollywood ain't holdin' its breath.

11
00:00:39,367 --> 00:00:42,532
Yeah, well, they're doin' it wrong.
I mean, for Hank.

12
00:00:42,605 --> 00:00:44,836
[Man]
Tell the director.
[Woman Laughs]

13
00:00:44,910 --> 00:00:48,906
I thought I'd give the marriage a few months
before I go for the meddling wife thing.

14
00:00:48,984 --> 00:00:52,444
His arm came back the day after
you hooked up. I say meddle.

15
00:00:52,524 --> 00:00:55,120
You okay?
Just gas.

16
00:00:55,196 --> 00:00:58,656
Go help your man. Give me
a little room here to work it out.

17
00:01:07,818 --> 00:01:10,584
Take it from me, Hank Wiggen.

18
00:01:10,656 --> 00:01:12,215
Like that?
No.

19
00:01:12,293 --> 00:01:14,285
Hey, sweetheart.
Hey.

20
00:01:15,298 --> 00:01:16,789
Hi, Bryan.
Hey.

21
00:01:16,869 --> 00:01:20,204
Having trouble with the big speech?
Yeah. You got any ideas?

22
00:01:20,274 --> 00:01:22,836
It's your story.
Just be yourself.

23
00:01:22,913 --> 00:01:26,373
Drugs were there, you took 'em.
Simple.

24
00:01:26,452 --> 00:01:29,685
Why'd you get clean?
'Cause I was gonna die.

25
00:01:29,758 --> 00:01:31,954
And, come April,
'cause you're clean,

26
00:01:32,029 --> 00:01:35,296
you're starting Opening Day
against the Yanks.

27
00:01:38,307 --> 00:01:40,173
Try it her way?
Yeah.

28
00:01:40,244 --> 00:01:42,179
Okay. Okay.

29
00:01:42,247 --> 00:01:46,778
Let's start with the second part first.
That'll get him in the groove.
Okay.

30
00:01:46,856 --> 00:01:48,848
We'll do the throwing thing first.

31
00:01:48,927 --> 00:01:50,919
Everybody wants to direct.

32
00:01:52,233 --> 00:01:54,931
- Warner all right?
- Yeah, he's good.

33
00:01:55,004 --> 00:01:58,601
You just bring it, babe.
Just tell your story.

34
00:01:58,678 --> 00:02:00,772
Roll cameras.

35
00:02:00,848 --> 00:02:02,817
Rolling.
Sound. Speed.

36
00:02:02,885 --> 00:02:06,084
Come on, kid.! Show 'em
what you're gonna give the Yankees.!

37
00:02:06,158 --> 00:02:07,820
All right, action!

38
00:02:19,048 --> 00:02:21,848
[Screaming, Groaning]

39
00:02:23,089 --> 00:02:25,285
[Groaning]
Oh, God!

40
00:02:33,775 --> 00:02:37,008
You okay?
It's gonna be okay. It's gonna be okay.

41
00:03:27,139 --> 00:03:31,010
He's got osteopenia. His bones
are too thin to fix the arm problem.

42
00:03:31,079 --> 00:03:35,018
No. Price is not a problem
if you have what I need.

43
00:03:35,086 --> 00:03:37,522
Young man?
How did you know?

44
00:03:37,591 --> 00:03:40,460
Well, if he's an old man,
osteopenia would just be a fact of life.

45
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:43,365
You make him comfortable, send him home,
which means you're just boring me.

46
00:03:43,435 --> 00:03:45,928
So he's young, which means
it's most likely caused by cancer.

47
00:03:46,006 --> 00:03:49,171
You're here because you haven't found it.
Have you looked really, really hard?

48
00:03:49,246 --> 00:03:51,716
M.R.I. And PET scan
are both negative.

49
00:03:51,784 --> 00:03:54,619
Well, how old is he?
Maybe the osteopenia is just early onset.

50
00:03:54,688 --> 00:03:57,089
Ah, let's see.

51
00:03:57,160 --> 00:04:00,188
"Born 9/21/77."

52
00:04:00,266 --> 00:04:01,757
It's Hank Wiggen?

53
00:04:03,338 --> 00:04:05,534
And he signed it. Sweet.
Yeah.

54
00:04:05,608 --> 00:04:09,604
"ToJimmy Wilson,
the Cy Young of medicine."

55
00:04:09,683 --> 00:04:12,677
Did you ask for that?
Just the "Jimmy" part.

56
00:04:13,957 --> 00:04:17,919
The bone's too thin to support the kind
of surgery that would let him pitch again.

57
00:04:17,998 --> 00:04:20,126
But if we figure out
what's causing the osteopenia,

58
00:04:20,202 --> 00:04:22,194
we can reverse the bone damage,
then do the surgery.

59
00:04:22,272 --> 00:04:25,766
Beat the Yankees
and save the free world.

60
00:04:30,154 --> 00:04:32,624
It was a working dinner.

61
00:04:32,692 --> 00:04:35,527
My work- Company pays.

62
00:04:36,599 --> 00:04:41,198
I don't know. I just feel kind of weird
after what it turned into.

63
00:04:41,274 --> 00:04:44,370
Well, then it stopped being work.

64
00:04:44,446 --> 00:04:47,781
You know, if it'll solve
your ethics problem,

65
00:04:48,821 --> 00:04:50,756
you can reimburse me for these.

66
00:04:50,825 --> 00:04:53,557
What are they, $5.57, I believe?

67
00:04:58,972 --> 00:05:01,670
Mmm.
Let me know about Friday?

68
00:05:01,745 --> 00:05:04,978
- Yeah.
- Mmm.

69
00:05:09,158 --> 00:05:11,150
[Exhales]

70
00:05:15,569 --> 00:05:17,561
[Door Closes]

71
00:05:23,952 --> 00:05:26,548
[Chuckles]

72
00:05:26,623 --> 00:05:28,524
[Chase]
None of the usual suspects.

73
00:05:28,593 --> 00:05:30,892
Age isn't right, in apparent
perfect health before this incident,

74
00:05:30,965 --> 00:05:34,562
M.R.I. And PET scan negative for tumors.
Test him again.
It's gotta be cancer.

75
00:05:34,638 --> 00:05:37,700
Sorry I'm late.
Car broke down on the interstate.

76
00:05:39,613 --> 00:05:43,518
Don't believe you.
CHEM-7 shows a poor kidney function.

77
00:05:43,587 --> 00:05:46,422
- Why would a guy in his 20s
have a poor kidney function?
- Cancer.

78
00:05:46,492 --> 00:05:49,554
It first attacks the bones,
and then the kidneys.

79
00:05:49,631 --> 00:05:54,572
Come on, people.
He was 17 and 7. His E.R.A. Was 2.1.

80
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:58,875
You want it to be his kidneys,
because if it's his kidneys,
then maybe we can treat it, fix it.

81
00:05:58,949 --> 00:06:01,784
And if it's cancer,
then he'll never pitch again.

82
00:06:01,854 --> 00:06:05,850
If this were a regular guy
who broke his arm lifting a box,
you would've sent him home.

83
00:06:05,927 --> 00:06:09,593
My God, you're right. I lost my head.
All life is equally sacred.

84
00:06:09,667 --> 00:06:14,232
I promise you. The next knitting injury
that comes in here, we're on it
like stink on cheese.

85
00:06:14,309 --> 00:06:18,408
- He weighed 175 his rookie year.
- Stop.

86
00:06:18,484 --> 00:06:20,578
Now he's 195
after playing a year in Japan.

87
00:06:20,654 --> 00:06:22,589
Why?
He let himself go.

88
00:06:22,658 --> 00:06:27,428
Steroids. The guy was a drug user.
I'm sure he wouldn't have balked
at pumping up through chemicals.

89
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:29,765
That'd explain the weight gain
and the kidney problems.

90
00:06:29,838 --> 00:06:32,673
And the bone loss.
Go ask him what he's on.

91
00:06:32,743 --> 00:06:35,839
When he says nothing,
have him pee in a cup.

92
00:06:38,687 --> 00:06:43,127
If your car breaks down,
you're an hour late, not two minutes.

93
00:06:43,196 --> 00:06:46,827
And two minutes isn't late enough
to use a clever excuse like car trouble.

94
00:06:46,902 --> 00:06:49,372
I was coming in early.
Huh.

95
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:52,104
Unprompted lies.
That's a bad sign.

96
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:56,481
Either a guilty conscience,
or something personal's going on.

97
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:04,229
See, that's all you had to do-
just walk in, sit down, do your job.

98
00:07:08,275 --> 00:07:10,676
No. No, I never took 'em.

99
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:13,840
We're gonna need a urine sample.

100
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:16,821
Oh, no, you don't trust me.

101
00:07:20,430 --> 00:07:22,422
Baby, I'm worried about
takin' this morphine.

102
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:23,991
You're in pain.

103
00:07:24,070 --> 00:07:27,166
The doses are monitored.
It's not a slip.

104
00:07:27,242 --> 00:07:29,234
Besides, opiates weren't your thing.

105
00:07:29,313 --> 00:07:32,284
They should've been.
Whoa.

106
00:07:32,351 --> 00:07:34,582
Mr. Wiggen? The urine sample.

107
00:07:35,658 --> 00:07:39,722
I wanna say no, so I am- no.

108
00:07:39,799 --> 00:07:44,466
Trust is a big issue in early recovery.
He really did gain the weight honestly.

109
00:07:45,709 --> 00:07:48,441
If you say so.

110
00:07:48,515 --> 00:07:50,313
You're not gettin' it.

111
00:07:52,121 --> 00:07:54,785
He thinks I'm an idiot.

112
00:07:56,028 --> 00:07:58,020
He sure does.

113
00:08:05,646 --> 00:08:07,342
Should we save a sample?

114
00:08:07,415 --> 00:08:11,115
Dr. Sports Fan can put it in Lucite
and hang it around his neck.

115
00:08:12,391 --> 00:08:14,884
Hey, Friday night,
can you cover for me?

116
00:08:14,963 --> 00:08:17,364
I think so.

117
00:08:17,434 --> 00:08:21,339
Oh, Friday. No, I'm sorry. I have to go
to that oncology thing, the seminar.

118
00:08:21,408 --> 00:08:23,775
Oh.
What's goin' on?

119
00:08:23,846 --> 00:08:25,781
Dinner with the drug rep.

120
00:08:25,849 --> 00:08:27,784
Castine Pharmaceuticals.

121
00:08:27,853 --> 00:08:31,622
Arnie?
Claims he has 500 lawyer jokes,
only tells one?

122
00:08:31,693 --> 00:08:34,596
Uh... new guy.

123
00:08:35,801 --> 00:08:37,861
You need cash?

124
00:08:39,408 --> 00:08:43,905
[Sighs]
No, l- I don't have that much on me.

125
00:08:43,982 --> 00:08:46,315
No, no, it's not a problem.

126
00:08:46,386 --> 00:08:48,514
I'll be over by 6:00. Okay.

127
00:08:49,526 --> 00:08:51,461
5:00 p.m. Dr. House checks out.

128
00:08:51,530 --> 00:08:54,899
It's 4:45.
I was rounding up.

129
00:08:54,968 --> 00:08:57,837
Carol Moffatt.
Please see Dr. House in Exam One.

130
00:08:57,908 --> 00:09:01,004
- Whoa, whoa, not so fast, Cathy.
- It's Carol.

131
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:04,176
Uh-
Uh, trouble with the leg?

132
00:09:05,922 --> 00:09:08,358
- When's the wedding?
- This Saturday.

133
00:09:08,426 --> 00:09:12,889
Ooh. Not much time
to fit into that pretty dress.
And no time for practical shoe shopping.

134
00:09:12,968 --> 00:09:16,406
- You're running two miles a day
further than you should be.
- It hurts right here-

135
00:09:16,475 --> 00:09:19,605
New shoes, less miles,
and ix-nay on the afternoon Cokes.
You're gonna look beautiful.

136
00:09:19,681 --> 00:09:22,550
- What's wrong with you?
- I can't get my contact lenses out.

137
00:09:22,619 --> 00:09:25,146
Out of what?
They're not in your eyes.

138
00:09:25,224 --> 00:09:28,389
- But they're red.
- That's because you're trying
to remove your corneas.

139
00:09:28,463 --> 00:09:31,229
What's wrong with you?
Uh, lately, my wife has noticed that-

140
00:09:31,301 --> 00:09:34,636
Yeah, yeah. Symptoms.
We're working on a personal best here.

141
00:09:34,708 --> 00:09:38,772
U-Uh, numbness in my feet
and hands, uh, constipation-

142
00:09:38,849 --> 00:09:42,048
And?
Maybe he doesn't feel comfortable
talking about his private matters.

143
00:09:42,121 --> 00:09:44,785
Well, neither would I if I was having
trouble controlling my pee-pee.

144
00:09:44,859 --> 00:09:47,796
You're a dentist.
Nitrous oxide poisoning.

145
00:09:47,865 --> 00:09:51,394
Which means you're either
dipping into your own supply
or you got a bad valve in the office.

146
00:09:51,472 --> 00:09:54,034
Laughing gas rehab's probably
more expensive than the plumber.

147
00:09:54,110 --> 00:09:56,409
Meanwhile, get yourself some B-12.

148
00:09:56,481 --> 00:09:58,473
Who's left?
I can't see.

149
00:10:01,690 --> 00:10:04,855
No, I'm just screwin' with you.
It's a hangover.

150
00:10:04,930 --> 00:10:08,493
My English lit prof told me
he'd fail me next time
if I didn't show up with a doctor's note.

151
00:10:08,570 --> 00:10:13,568
Well, make friends with the dentist.
He can give you a note, and maybe
a little nitrous to take the edge off.

152
00:10:16,518 --> 00:10:18,453
[Cameron]
Dr. House.

153
00:10:18,521 --> 00:10:20,456
He tested negative for steroids.

154
00:10:20,525 --> 00:10:22,460
Elevated beta-2 proteins though.

155
00:10:22,528 --> 00:10:25,363
Could be cancerous-
amyloidosis or lymphoma.

156
00:10:25,434 --> 00:10:27,335
Or steroids.
You guys got any money on you?

157
00:10:27,403 --> 00:10:29,338
He tested negative for steroids.

158
00:10:29,407 --> 00:10:31,569
I have a couple 20s on me.
Fifty of'em?

159
00:10:31,645 --> 00:10:36,780
Foreman?
The fat-pad biopsy and abdominal C.T. Scan
were negative for the cancers, but-

160
00:10:36,854 --> 00:10:39,324
That just leaves us
with steroids.

161
00:10:39,392 --> 00:10:41,384
He tested negative for steroids.

162
00:10:41,463 --> 00:10:44,025
Less money is made by biochemists
working on a cure for cancer...

163
00:10:44,101 --> 00:10:48,200
than by their colleagues struggling valiantly
to find ways to hide steroid use.

164
00:10:49,277 --> 00:10:51,770
But there is one thing
they can't hide.

165
00:10:57,792 --> 00:11:00,456
Hi. I'm Dr. House.

166
00:11:00,531 --> 00:11:03,832
And this is the coolest day of my life.

167
00:11:07,644 --> 00:11:09,510
[Clears Throat]

168
00:11:09,581 --> 00:11:11,948
See?
Steroid use shrinks the testicles.

169
00:11:13,689 --> 00:11:16,159
I'm clean, man.
No steroids, no nothin'.

170
00:11:16,226 --> 00:11:19,823
Your lips say no,
your prunes say yes.

171
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:22,769
Hypogonadism.
Isn't that a great word?

172
00:11:22,838 --> 00:11:26,937
Thanks. We don't get
to say it nearly enough.
Start him on Lupron right away.

173
00:11:30,018 --> 00:11:33,285
These freaks are willing
to defile themselves
for mass entertainment.

174
00:11:33,358 --> 00:11:36,261
For money.
I feel sorry for them.

175
00:11:36,329 --> 00:11:38,891
He drops a clean urine,
denies using steroids.

176
00:11:38,967 --> 00:11:42,132
And you're giving him a drug
for what, steroid abuse?

177
00:11:42,207 --> 00:11:45,474
No, no, it's not.
It's got calcium in it.

178
00:11:45,546 --> 00:11:47,913
It's very good for the bones.

179
00:11:47,984 --> 00:11:50,146
Basically, at a molecular level,
it's just milk.

180
00:11:50,222 --> 00:11:52,316
[Sighs]

181
00:11:52,392 --> 00:11:54,919
[Woman On P.A.]
Dr. Whitman to Anesthesiology.
Dr. Whitman, Anesthesiology.

182
00:11:54,997 --> 00:11:57,832
How long do you figure
before I get a call from Cuddy?

183
00:11:57,902 --> 00:12:00,771
- [Cuddy] You put him on Lupron?
- Uh-huh.

184
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:03,105
- And you told them it was like milk.
- Yes.

185
00:12:03,178 --> 00:12:06,240
Is there any way
in which that is not a lie?

186
00:12:07,486 --> 00:12:09,478
It's creamy.

187
00:12:09,556 --> 00:12:11,718
- But I had three reasons.
- Good ones?

188
00:12:11,794 --> 00:12:15,129
Well, we'll see in a minute.
I'm just making them up now.

189
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:18,797
- He lied to me first.
- Your mother did teach you
two wrongs don't make a right.

190
00:12:18,873 --> 00:12:22,903
Lfhe lies to me about not taking steroids,
and I lie to him about not treating steroids,
he's cured.

191
00:12:22,981 --> 00:12:24,779
Adds up for me.
Second reason.

192
00:12:24,851 --> 00:12:27,116
If I told him the truth,
he wouldn't have taken the stuff.

193
00:12:27,189 --> 00:12:30,160
And if he told you the truth,
what would the stuff do to him?

194
00:12:30,227 --> 00:12:32,594
- Severe respiratory problems.
- Third reason?

195
00:12:32,665 --> 00:12:35,295
I wanted to eliminate
the placebo effect.

196
00:12:35,370 --> 00:12:37,464
Excellent.

197
00:12:37,541 --> 00:12:40,341
You and your lawyer
can write a paper.

198
00:12:40,413 --> 00:12:43,646
Which brings me to my fourth reason.
I thought you said
there were only three.

199
00:12:43,719 --> 00:12:46,018
- I thought you'd buy one of'em.
- Seriously?

200
00:12:46,090 --> 00:12:47,649
He's not gonna sue.

201
00:12:47,726 --> 00:12:49,695
Because his lawyer is a nice guy...

202
00:12:49,764 --> 00:12:54,033
who'll realize it's unfair to blame us
for ruining this kid's $100 million career.

203
00:12:54,104 --> 00:12:56,039
Good guess, but no.

204
00:12:56,108 --> 00:13:00,104
If the Lupron causes respiratory problems,
it means he's not on steroids.

205
00:13:00,182 --> 00:13:03,483
Which means there's
something else wrong with him.

206
00:13:03,555 --> 00:13:06,219
And the choices
for that something else...

207
00:13:06,293 --> 00:13:09,696
are almost universally very bad.

208
00:13:09,766 --> 00:13:12,202
[Wheezing]

209
00:13:15,677 --> 00:13:18,671
[Gasping, Wheezing Intensifies]

210
00:13:31,272 --> 00:13:33,799
[House]
Osteopenia, messing his bones up.

211
00:13:33,877 --> 00:13:38,408
Hypogonadism,
impaired liver function,
kidney function.

212
00:13:38,485 --> 00:13:42,082
And we have managed to find
the only professional athlete in the galaxy...

213
00:13:42,159 --> 00:13:44,219
who is not on steroids.

214
00:13:44,295 --> 00:13:46,230
And it's not cancer.

215
00:13:46,299 --> 00:13:48,234
So what's killing him?

216
00:13:48,303 --> 00:13:51,331
Who shares my suspicions
that the Yankees were somehow involved?

217
00:13:51,408 --> 00:13:55,313
Shrunken testicles indicate his body's
not putting out enough testosterone.

218
00:13:55,383 --> 00:14:00,119
Throw out the lungs.
That was the Lupron-my fault.
Don't worry. I'll send him a nice note.

219
00:14:00,191 --> 00:14:01,454
What about something environmental?

220
00:14:01,527 --> 00:14:03,997
Arsenic, mercury.
The symptoms could indicate-

221
00:14:04,065 --> 00:14:06,729
Pretty small environment.
Wife's fine, no one else is sick.

222
00:14:06,803 --> 00:14:09,399
If you throw out the kidneys,
everything else adds up.

223
00:14:09,475 --> 00:14:11,968
The testicles, the bones,
the impaired liver function...

224
00:14:12,046 --> 00:14:14,744
could all be caused
by a breakdown
of his adrenal glands.

225
00:14:14,818 --> 00:14:16,980
Addison's disease. I like it.

226
00:14:17,055 --> 00:14:18,990
Mainly, of course,
because the treatment is-

227
00:14:19,059 --> 00:14:22,258
- Steroids.
- Enough irony for all of us.

228
00:14:22,332 --> 00:14:23,925
Treatment would cause him
to retain fluid.

229
00:14:24,001 --> 00:14:28,134
- With the kidneys almost
shut down already, he'll die.
- So we'll get him a new kidney.

230
00:14:28,209 --> 00:14:31,408
Your theory is that Addison's
is causing all the symptoms...

231
00:14:31,481 --> 00:14:33,473
except for the kidney problems.

232
00:14:33,552 --> 00:14:37,889
- What's causing the kidney problems?
- Cameron, if you had to make
an ironic guess right about now-

233
00:14:37,961 --> 00:14:40,397
[Cameron, Chase]
He tested negative for steroids.

234
00:14:40,465 --> 00:14:42,958
Agreed.
He's not on steroids now.

235
00:14:43,036 --> 00:14:46,702
But if he was on them
at any time in the last five years,
it could have caused the kidney damage.

236
00:14:49,281 --> 00:14:52,878
You see, kidneys don't wear watches.

237
00:14:52,954 --> 00:14:57,417
Sure, gall bladders do, but it doesn't matter,
'cause kidneys can't tell time.

238
00:14:59,132 --> 00:15:01,694
Steroid damage could take years.

239
00:15:01,770 --> 00:15:04,001
No steroids. How many times
does he have to tell you?

240
00:15:04,074 --> 00:15:05,940
I don't know.

241
00:15:06,012 --> 00:15:08,949
How many times did he lie about cocaine
before coming clean with the league?

242
00:15:09,017 --> 00:15:11,920
- That's completely different.
- Oh, that's right, I remember.

243
00:15:11,989 --> 00:15:16,953
You never did come clean.
The league was out to get you.
They faked the blood tests.

244
00:15:17,032 --> 00:15:18,967
You had to get yourself
a lawyer and everything.

245
00:15:19,035 --> 00:15:22,666
If Hank says he never used steroids,
that's the truth.

246
00:15:22,741 --> 00:15:28,411
That's too bad,
because our theory is that
the kidney damage is caused by "A, '"

247
00:15:28,485 --> 00:15:30,420
and everything else
is caused by "B."

248
00:15:30,489 --> 00:15:33,460
The beauty of this theory is
that we can treat "A" and "B."

249
00:15:33,528 --> 00:15:36,988
But if you add the kidney symptoms
back into the mix,

250
00:15:37,068 --> 00:15:39,937
then we are looking
at another letter altogether,

251
00:15:40,007 --> 00:15:41,942
one that is apparently
not in the alphabet.

252
00:15:42,010 --> 00:15:46,609
We can't fix the bones,
no more baseball, no more breathing,

253
00:15:46,685 --> 00:15:48,620
no more brain function.

254
00:15:50,325 --> 00:15:52,260
Get another explanation.

255
00:15:52,329 --> 00:15:55,823
Okay. Yeah, I think I got one
in my other pants.

256
00:15:55,902 --> 00:15:58,303
Hold on.

257
00:16:01,612 --> 00:16:03,547
Five years ago. Bangor, Maine.

258
00:16:04,852 --> 00:16:07,721
My pitching coach had me on something.
I never knew what it was.

259
00:16:08,758 --> 00:16:12,527
And you never tried too hard
to find out either.

260
00:16:13,734 --> 00:16:16,466
I gained twelve pounds of muscle
in, like, four weeks.

261
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:18,372
I'm sorry, baby.

262
00:16:21,081 --> 00:16:23,073
Huh?

263
00:16:24,621 --> 00:16:27,649
How ya doin', Doc?
Good. Very good, yeah.

264
00:16:32,335 --> 00:16:35,534
You want me to put Hank Wiggen
on the transplant list.

265
00:16:35,607 --> 00:16:38,772
He needs a new kidney. I was thinking
the kidney people might have some.

266
00:16:38,847 --> 00:16:43,754
They like to save them for people who have-
How do I put this? Kidney problems.

267
00:16:43,822 --> 00:16:46,691
He's a professional ball player.
Brings joy to millions.

268
00:16:46,762 --> 00:16:49,927
Do you really want to be known as
the hospital that sent him home to die?

269
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:53,369
That's a great idea.
We could be the hospital
that killed two people-

270
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:56,934
the guy who deserved the kidney,
and the ball player we bumped up the list...

271
00:16:57,013 --> 00:16:58,948
when we weren't even sure
what was wrong with him.

272
00:16:59,017 --> 00:17:00,747
Everything else
is related to the Addison's.

273
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:03,051
The test for Addison's
was inconclusive.

274
00:17:03,124 --> 00:17:05,924
The test for Addison's
is always inconclusive.

275
00:17:05,996 --> 00:17:08,592
Why do we do it at all?
We should just ask you.

276
00:17:14,713 --> 00:17:16,648
You're not putting him on the list.

277
00:17:16,716 --> 00:17:19,346
Your powers of deduction
are breathtaking.

278
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:23,257
- You take a perverse pleasure
in turning me down.
- What I live for.

279
00:17:24,797 --> 00:17:30,205
Once in a while, though, try to ruin my day-
ask me something I can say "Yes" to.

280
00:17:46,937 --> 00:17:50,876
Oh, I'm sorry, Doctor.
I didn't know you were busy.
Want me to come back?

281
00:17:50,944 --> 00:17:54,177
- Is he on the list?
- No.

282
00:17:54,251 --> 00:17:57,552
- Then I'm giving him one of mine.
- Okay.

283
00:17:57,624 --> 00:18:00,925
You're not gonna tell me it's a bad idea?
Why give a kidney to someone
who might not be able to use it?

284
00:18:00,997 --> 00:18:03,661
Not my area.

285
00:18:03,735 --> 00:18:05,727
That is, however, my chair.

286
00:18:06,940 --> 00:18:08,875
When do we do it?

287
00:18:08,944 --> 00:18:11,209
Very noble gesture.

288
00:18:11,282 --> 00:18:15,051
My favorite kind.
Dramatic, yet completely empty.

289
00:18:15,122 --> 00:18:17,250
The chances of nonidentical twins
being a match-

290
00:18:17,326 --> 00:18:19,261
You live alone?
You writing a book?

291
00:18:19,330 --> 00:18:22,392
I made it a question
just 'cause it's more polite.

292
00:18:22,469 --> 00:18:24,802
You got a big "keep out" sign
stapled on your forehead.

293
00:18:24,873 --> 00:18:27,469
That explains it.
I told 'em to put it on my door.

294
00:18:27,544 --> 00:18:32,815
Even if real human contact is something
you don't have or even want or need,

295
00:18:32,888 --> 00:18:35,119
you should at least be able
to see it in other people.

296
00:18:35,192 --> 00:18:36,660
Yeah. Right.

297
00:18:36,728 --> 00:18:40,063
True love- that's just how
we match organs these days.

298
00:18:40,135 --> 00:18:43,801
There's a couple in France-
high school sweethearts-
they're trading brains.

299
00:18:45,043 --> 00:18:47,741
We're a match. Run your tests.

300
00:18:53,426 --> 00:18:55,588
[Pager Buzzing]

301
00:19:02,241 --> 00:19:04,711
Hey. The lab call?
Is she a match?

302
00:19:04,779 --> 00:19:06,714
Haven't heard yet.

303
00:19:06,783 --> 00:19:10,221
You got a text message, though.
"Friday night." Very cryptic.

304
00:19:10,290 --> 00:19:13,193
Gee, thanks for checking.
Can you cover for me?

305
00:19:13,261 --> 00:19:15,594
Oncology seminar.
Right.

306
00:19:15,666 --> 00:19:18,330
Friday night the same thing
as the car trouble?

307
00:19:18,404 --> 00:19:20,236
I had car trouble.

308
00:19:20,308 --> 00:19:23,108
House says you were lying.
I believe him.

309
00:19:23,179 --> 00:19:26,879
What's that?
You got a little wet smudge
at the end of your nose.

310
00:19:26,953 --> 00:19:29,583
Hey, I like the guy.
He says what he wants,
does what he wants.

311
00:19:29,658 --> 00:19:32,254
He won't talk to anyone
unless he can jerk them around.

312
00:19:32,330 --> 00:19:35,096
Or needs a thousand bucks.
What is with that?

313
00:19:35,168 --> 00:19:37,262
I scored.

314
00:19:39,208 --> 00:19:41,336
It's a brave new world, Doc,

315
00:19:41,412 --> 00:19:43,643
and we are the cutting edge.

316
00:19:45,654 --> 00:19:49,787
You are looking
at two all-access passes...

317
00:19:49,861 --> 00:19:51,591
to paradise itself.

318
00:19:52,867 --> 00:19:56,704
How much?
True cost?
No man can say.

319
00:19:56,774 --> 00:19:58,868
Could that man's accountant say?

320
00:19:58,945 --> 00:20:01,210
One thousand dollars.
Whew.

321
00:20:01,283 --> 00:20:05,313
Friday night.
The biggest official monster truck jam
in the history of New Jersey.

322
00:20:06,725 --> 00:20:09,753
Okay, please tell me
you didn't just say Friday night.

323
00:20:09,831 --> 00:20:12,802
Whatever you've got, you cancel.
[Stammering]

324
00:20:12,870 --> 00:20:15,773
I can't do it.
They only give these tickets
to owners.

325
00:20:15,842 --> 00:20:19,280
Anytime we wanna be
in the middle of the track,
we're in the middle of the track.

326
00:20:19,348 --> 00:20:23,151
These tickets are so good,
we have to sign a release.

327
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:25,784
I mean it.
We do this, we could die.

328
00:20:25,860 --> 00:20:29,354
I've got the oncology thing.
L- l-

329
00:20:29,434 --> 00:20:33,305
The rectal cancer lecture-
they booked me a year ago.
L-l-l-l-I can't get out.

330
00:20:33,374 --> 00:20:35,366
There's no way out.

331
00:20:36,412 --> 00:20:39,781
Fine.
I'll ask one of my other friends.

332
00:20:39,852 --> 00:20:41,946
Huh.

333
00:20:43,192 --> 00:20:45,719
What? You're saying
I've only got one friend?

334
00:20:45,796 --> 00:20:49,826
Uh... and wh-who-

335
00:20:51,707 --> 00:20:53,642
Kevin in Bookkeeping.

336
00:20:54,712 --> 00:20:56,510
Okay, well, first of all,
his name's Carl.

337
00:20:56,583 --> 00:20:58,643
I call him Kevin.

338
00:20:58,720 --> 00:21:01,418
It's his secret friendship club name.

339
00:21:02,427 --> 00:21:05,330
It's hookers.
[Cameron]
Oh, my God.!

340
00:21:05,399 --> 00:21:09,361
Multiple hookers. But House is House.
He's gotta have it his way.
Four or five women.

341
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:12,707
This isn't even funny.
What?
You don't think he has sex?

342
00:21:12,779 --> 00:21:16,273
- No, of course he-
- He doesn't have sex, he makes love.

343
00:21:16,352 --> 00:21:18,287
[Laughing]
I didn't say that.

344
00:21:18,356 --> 00:21:20,849
[Buzzing]

345
00:21:20,927 --> 00:21:22,725
It's the lab.

346
00:21:22,798 --> 00:21:24,528
Dr. Foreman.

347
00:21:25,602 --> 00:21:28,573
[Man On P.A.]
Respiratory Therapy, call 4702.

348
00:21:28,641 --> 00:21:31,042
Respiratory Therapy,
pick up 4702.

349
00:21:31,112 --> 00:21:36,053
If you have the results,
I'd like you to talk to both of us.
If you don't, I'm late for a meeting.

350
00:21:36,122 --> 00:21:39,582
Believe me. I'd much rather
be with your better half.

351
00:21:39,661 --> 00:21:43,498
And by better half, I mean the one who
struck out Sammy Sosa on three pitches...

352
00:21:43,569 --> 00:21:45,936
and talks a lot less.

353
00:21:46,006 --> 00:21:49,945
But I thought I would
talk to you first and alone.

354
00:21:50,013 --> 00:21:53,178
I got your results back from the lab.

355
00:21:53,253 --> 00:21:55,449
You do match.

356
00:21:55,523 --> 00:21:57,685
L- I do?

357
00:22:03,271 --> 00:22:05,502
You're also pregnant.

358
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:14,287
You can't be a donor.

359
00:22:17,396 --> 00:22:19,456
Not in your current condition.

360
00:22:30,420 --> 00:22:33,619
Um... excuse me.

361
00:22:33,693 --> 00:22:36,129
I have to go talk to my husband.

362
00:22:51,793 --> 00:22:54,263
[Printer Beeping]

363
00:22:57,336 --> 00:23:00,034
Heart looks good.
We can schedule the transplant.

364
00:23:00,108 --> 00:23:01,872
No transplant.

365
00:23:01,944 --> 00:23:04,311
Lola's not gonna have an abortion.

366
00:23:04,382 --> 00:23:07,979
Actually, your wife just told me
that she was making an appointment.

367
00:23:08,055 --> 00:23:10,251
I don't care what she said.

368
00:23:10,326 --> 00:23:12,990
I think you two
need to discuss this further.

369
00:23:13,064 --> 00:23:16,092
We've been trying to get pregnant
almost since we met.

370
00:23:16,170 --> 00:23:19,232
Well, it's your wife's decision
whether or not-

371
00:23:19,309 --> 00:23:22,337
She wants to trade a child
for a kidney. That's murder.

372
00:23:22,415 --> 00:23:24,407
I'm not gonna let her do that.

373
00:23:27,424 --> 00:23:30,361
Foreman says we've got a problem
about the transplant.

374
00:23:30,430 --> 00:23:35,303
If she terminates the pregnancy,
he's not gonna let himself die on principle.

375
00:23:35,372 --> 00:23:38,309
Would you give up a baby
for someone you love?

376
00:23:39,813 --> 00:23:42,978
Please tell me I don't have to decide.

377
00:23:43,053 --> 00:23:46,115
It depends.
How long would they live?

378
00:23:46,192 --> 00:23:49,459
This is a pragmatic question
for you?

379
00:23:49,531 --> 00:23:51,466
Fifty years, no problem.

380
00:23:51,535 --> 00:23:53,971
Six months, I say let him die.

381
00:23:54,039 --> 00:23:59,310
I've actually given this a lot of thought.
My personal tipping point is
seven years, eight months and 14 days.

382
00:23:59,382 --> 00:24:00,975
I couldn't do it.

383
00:24:01,052 --> 00:24:02,987
You found religion?

384
00:24:03,055 --> 00:24:06,584
- Do you have to be religious
to believe a fetus is a life?
- There seems to be a correlation.

385
00:24:13,775 --> 00:24:15,937
I'm, uh-
[Sighs]

386
00:24:18,484 --> 00:24:20,077
Do you like monster trucks?

387
00:24:21,957 --> 00:24:24,553
- I don't know what they are.
- Right.

388
00:24:26,932 --> 00:24:29,732
I got two tickets.
Friday night.

389
00:24:30,739 --> 00:24:34,610
- You asking me to go with you?
- Sure. Sounds good.

390
00:24:34,679 --> 00:24:37,411
Like a date?

391
00:24:37,485 --> 00:24:39,477
Exactly.

392
00:24:39,555 --> 00:24:41,547
Except for the- the date part.

393
00:24:43,363 --> 00:24:45,594
Forget it.

394
00:24:45,666 --> 00:24:50,402
Uh, no, l- I was gonna go
to the oncology dinner.

395
00:24:50,475 --> 00:24:53,844
Of course. You have to
hear Wilson's lecture.

396
00:24:53,915 --> 00:24:56,909
No. I just found out he canceled,
like, two weeks ago.

397
00:25:03,499 --> 00:25:06,868
So... what do I wear?

398
00:25:09,343 --> 00:25:11,539
Still with us, Hank?
Yeah. I'm here.

399
00:25:11,614 --> 00:25:14,050
My chest feels funny.

400
00:25:14,119 --> 00:25:16,851
Tachycardia.
Your heart's beating too fast.

401
00:25:16,923 --> 00:25:19,485
We're sorting it out.
But you stay with us, all right?

402
00:25:20,897 --> 00:25:22,798
- Keep talking to us, Hank!
- Where's Lola?

403
00:25:22,868 --> 00:25:26,397
Ten units of insulin sub-Q.
An I.V. Push D-50.

404
00:25:26,474 --> 00:25:28,910
- Why's his potassium up?
- Damned if I know.

405
00:25:28,979 --> 00:25:32,041
Kayexalate too. We gotta suck
that potassium out of him.
We gotta get his heart rate down.

406
00:25:32,118 --> 00:25:34,212
- [Woman] We need a crash cart!
- You got it.

407
00:25:34,288 --> 00:25:36,689
[Monitor Alarm Beeping]

408
00:25:36,759 --> 00:25:39,252
- It's definitely not Addison's.
- It's not steroids either.

409
00:25:39,331 --> 00:25:42,666
Set.
Help in here, please!

410
00:25:42,737 --> 00:25:47,302
His heart rate is 130 and rising
like a RandyJohnson line drives.

411
00:25:48,514 --> 00:25:51,417
"A" for effort.
There's no point
in doing the transplant.

412
00:25:51,487 --> 00:25:55,927
Even if he was stable enough,
it's obvious that we have no idea
what's wrong with him.

413
00:25:55,994 --> 00:25:59,694
First it's too high.
Now it's too low?

414
00:26:01,138 --> 00:26:04,473
His heart's not responding
to the atropine.

415
00:26:04,543 --> 00:26:07,605
Heart rate's down to 40.
I thought it was up.

416
00:26:07,683 --> 00:26:10,119
Now it's down.
Last time he went out at 35.

417
00:26:10,187 --> 00:26:12,987
- What's wrong?
- I have no idea.

418
00:26:14,896 --> 00:26:18,163
Hit him with the atropine
before he gets to 35 again.

419
00:26:19,538 --> 00:26:21,632
[Foreman]
We've already given him
three milliliters.

420
00:26:21,708 --> 00:26:23,802
[House]
Apparently that's not enough.

421
00:26:24,814 --> 00:26:26,749
[Chase]
We can't stabilize his heart rate.

422
00:26:26,818 --> 00:26:28,753
[House]
What did you do to him?
Kayexalate.

423
00:26:28,821 --> 00:26:31,815
His pulse was through the roof.
So was his potassium.

424
00:26:31,893 --> 00:26:35,296
- It wouldn't do this.
- Something did.

425
00:26:38,906 --> 00:26:42,105
Call me when he's stable.
Or dead.

426
00:26:51,929 --> 00:26:54,194
I remember the first time.

427
00:26:55,469 --> 00:26:58,235
You weren't even supposed
to be pitching that day.

428
00:26:58,309 --> 00:27:00,745
I'd flown all the way to Tokyo
to watch this kid,

429
00:27:00,813 --> 00:27:04,877
and he gets tossed
for arguing a call in the first inning.

430
00:27:06,623 --> 00:27:10,687
Ah, your pitches- perfect.

431
00:27:11,700 --> 00:27:14,603
Ball seemed to go faster
than your arm.

432
00:27:14,671 --> 00:27:19,703
It was like the rules didn't apply,
like physics couldn't slow you down.

433
00:27:20,749 --> 00:27:22,980
Hot damn, it was beautiful.

434
00:27:26,526 --> 00:27:28,188
Hey, Warner.

435
00:27:29,866 --> 00:27:32,632
Hey, kid. How ya feelin'?

436
00:27:32,704 --> 00:27:35,266
I hurt.

437
00:27:35,342 --> 00:27:38,472
My arm, my head, everywhere.

438
00:27:39,717 --> 00:27:42,415
They must've dialed down
the morphine.

439
00:27:42,489 --> 00:27:45,483
That's just wrong, man.
You're in pain.

440
00:27:46,529 --> 00:27:49,932
Hey, I got somethin' for ya.

441
00:27:52,006 --> 00:27:54,100
No.

442
00:27:54,177 --> 00:27:57,376
A doc in St. Louis
gave 'em to me for migraine.

443
00:27:57,449 --> 00:28:01,320
I'm an addict. I can't take that.
Even Lola was okay with the morphine.

444
00:28:01,389 --> 00:28:04,019
This stuff's just a little stronger.

445
00:28:04,095 --> 00:28:06,087
Come on.

446
00:28:11,642 --> 00:28:14,112
I'll just try one, Warner.

447
00:28:15,115 --> 00:28:18,952
[Man On P.A.]
Dr. Mulvaney,
please call extension 6134.

448
00:28:19,022 --> 00:28:22,152
Dr. Mulvaney,
please call extension 6134.

449
00:28:22,228 --> 00:28:24,561
Three more symptoms.

450
00:28:24,632 --> 00:28:27,330
Heart rate up. Heart rate down.

451
00:28:27,404 --> 00:28:30,375
Now he's hallucinating.
You gotta promise not to tell Lola.

452
00:28:31,377 --> 00:28:34,314
Okay, coach?
He's not just dreaming?

453
00:28:34,383 --> 00:28:37,752
No R.E.M.
He's actually awake.

454
00:28:37,822 --> 00:28:40,349
Drugs?
Not psychedelics.

455
00:28:40,428 --> 00:28:42,955
Not with the heart symptoms.

456
00:28:43,032 --> 00:28:47,438
Well, hallucinations
would point to digitalis.
It would also mess up his heart.

457
00:28:47,507 --> 00:28:49,772
But he's not on it.

458
00:28:49,844 --> 00:28:52,474
And why would he take it?

459
00:28:53,684 --> 00:28:55,550
Yeah.

460
00:28:55,622 --> 00:28:57,716
Pithy analysis.

461
00:28:57,792 --> 00:29:00,729
I can see why they asked you
to speak at the cancer dinner.

462
00:29:00,797 --> 00:29:02,993
I'm sorry I'm gonna miss it.

463
00:29:03,068 --> 00:29:05,264
I'm sorry
about the monster trucks.

464
00:29:05,339 --> 00:29:08,435
No, I think it's great.
You're giving back.

465
00:29:10,983 --> 00:29:13,316
Only thing is...

466
00:29:15,391 --> 00:29:17,383
uh, digitalis,

467
00:29:18,931 --> 00:29:21,697
it would only explain
the later symptoms,

468
00:29:21,770 --> 00:29:23,762
not the original ones.

469
00:29:33,023 --> 00:29:36,392
Sure, you know,
it's got a lot of movement.

470
00:29:36,463 --> 00:29:38,398
Problem is,
everybody sees the movement.

471
00:29:38,466 --> 00:29:41,869
You're throwin' your curveball
like you're-you're throwin' a curveball.

472
00:29:41,939 --> 00:29:45,536
Deception.
That's the-
[Coach Yelling Instructions]

473
00:29:45,613 --> 00:29:47,548
Same motion.

474
00:29:47,617 --> 00:29:50,554
Less movement,
but it won't come back at you.

475
00:29:50,622 --> 00:29:53,616
[Coach]
All right, outfielders move in.!
Right there.!

476
00:29:56,633 --> 00:29:58,363
How'd you get in here?

477
00:29:58,436 --> 00:30:02,033
Spoke Spanish.
Told them I was the new shortstop
from the Dominican.

478
00:30:02,110 --> 00:30:04,808
How's Hank doin'?
Lousy.

479
00:30:06,685 --> 00:30:11,854
Around your fingernails,
that swelling, it's called clubbing.

480
00:30:11,927 --> 00:30:14,921
Hippocrates noticed that a lot
of his friends who also had that...

481
00:30:14,999 --> 00:30:17,663
tended to frequently
grab their chests and die.

482
00:30:17,738 --> 00:30:20,834
Yeah, I got a heart condition.
What's wrong with Hank?

483
00:30:20,910 --> 00:30:23,175
What do you take for it?
Digitalis.

484
00:30:23,248 --> 00:30:25,240
Got 'em with you?

485
00:30:26,621 --> 00:30:29,558
Huh.
Well, that's weird.

486
00:30:29,626 --> 00:30:33,725
I just filled this prescription
a couple days ago.
There's another bottle here.

487
00:30:33,801 --> 00:30:35,861
Don't bother.

488
00:30:35,938 --> 00:30:38,773
Hank Wiggen stole your pills.

489
00:30:38,843 --> 00:30:40,709
He tried to kill himself.

490
00:30:57,376 --> 00:30:59,368
So what happened?

491
00:31:00,816 --> 00:31:03,753
He left the bottle open
while he went to get some water?

492
00:31:03,822 --> 00:31:05,757
Next time,
just take the whole bottle.

493
00:31:06,761 --> 00:31:09,493
Hey, man, you got no right.

494
00:31:09,565 --> 00:31:12,400
See, people remember
how many they've got.

495
00:31:12,471 --> 00:31:16,000
Date's right on the label,
number of pills-
regular person can do the math.

496
00:31:16,078 --> 00:31:20,313
But a junkie doesn't have to,
because how many pills he's got left,
that's all he's thinking about.

497
00:31:21,387 --> 00:31:23,322
Big insurance policy?

498
00:31:23,391 --> 00:31:25,087
[Laughs]

499
00:31:25,161 --> 00:31:29,032
- This isn't about the money.
- Not for you, no.

500
00:31:29,101 --> 00:31:33,336
Most reputable stores won't
cash your checks after you're dead.

501
00:31:33,409 --> 00:31:37,143
But for Lola, well, girls like that,
they're all about the money.

502
00:31:37,216 --> 00:31:39,344
Don't you say that.

503
00:31:39,420 --> 00:31:42,186
She already saved my life.

504
00:31:42,258 --> 00:31:45,661
I was dead in Japan. She brought me back.
Everything since then, that's gravy.

505
00:31:45,731 --> 00:31:47,529
That's more than I deserve.

506
00:31:47,602 --> 00:31:49,537
You owe her?
Everything.

507
00:31:49,605 --> 00:31:51,665
Ah. So the attempted suicide,

508
00:31:51,742 --> 00:31:55,772
the scaring her to death-
what is that? That's gratitude?

509
00:31:55,850 --> 00:31:57,716
Love?

510
00:31:57,787 --> 00:31:59,813
Yeah, I get that.

511
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:06,231
Well, take out
what you did to yourself yesterday-
we're back to the kidneys and the bones.

512
00:32:08,005 --> 00:32:09,906
I'm scheduling the transplant.

513
00:32:11,511 --> 00:32:14,539
- [Grunting]
- [Urine Sloshing, Dripping]

514
00:32:16,020 --> 00:32:18,148
Never visit a patient.

515
00:32:18,224 --> 00:32:19,817
I want that baby!

516
00:32:19,894 --> 00:32:22,797
Even if I'm gone,
that's a piece of me and Lola...

517
00:32:22,866 --> 00:32:25,666
breathing, walking around town,

518
00:32:25,738 --> 00:32:27,730
goin'to baseball games.

519
00:32:29,778 --> 00:32:33,444
If there's any more transplant talk
from you, Lola, or anybody else,

520
00:32:34,453 --> 00:32:36,946
I won't screw it up this time.

521
00:32:37,025 --> 00:32:39,017
I'll take myself out for good.

522
00:32:42,568 --> 00:32:47,600
I'll start treating the Addison's,
which will most likely destroy
what's left of your kidneys.

523
00:32:47,678 --> 00:32:50,308
Fine.
Start the treatment.

524
00:32:50,382 --> 00:32:52,442
[Bell Dings]

525
00:32:56,962 --> 00:32:58,954
Hey.

526
00:33:00,702 --> 00:33:03,639
What-
Hank Wiggen peed on me.

527
00:33:03,707 --> 00:33:06,507
What do you think these pants
are worth on eBay?

528
00:33:06,579 --> 00:33:09,982
I've got some big boy diapers in my office.
The rep hands 'em out like candy.

529
00:33:10,051 --> 00:33:13,386
Is it that bad?
No, not if you like
the smell of urine.

530
00:33:13,458 --> 00:33:17,454
Of course, why should I
trust someone who lies
about what he's doing Friday night?

531
00:33:19,068 --> 00:33:22,005
Question is, what are you
really doing Friday night?

532
00:33:22,073 --> 00:33:26,137
Or more to the point,
what could possibly be better
than monster trucks?

533
00:33:26,215 --> 00:33:28,207
Or are we breaking up?

534
00:33:32,760 --> 00:33:34,752
[Sighs]

535
00:33:45,617 --> 00:33:48,588
Stacy's coming into town
this weekend.

536
00:33:48,655 --> 00:33:50,590
We're having dinner.

537
00:33:50,659 --> 00:33:52,651
Just catching up.

538
00:33:54,066 --> 00:33:56,092
I definitely had pants here.

539
00:33:56,169 --> 00:33:58,969
Wait a second.
Is that Stacy the stripper?

540
00:33:59,041 --> 00:34:00,976
I heard she's playing Atlantic City.

541
00:34:01,044 --> 00:34:05,347
No, Stacy the constitutional lawyer.

542
00:34:06,354 --> 00:34:08,482
You thought
I couldn't handle this news.

543
00:34:12,432 --> 00:34:14,424
You talk to her a lot?

544
00:34:15,504 --> 00:34:18,737
No, it's been a long time.

545
00:34:21,248 --> 00:34:25,813
- If you don't want me to see her-
- What is this, eighth grade? I'm fine.

546
00:34:25,890 --> 00:34:27,825
It's fine if you're upset.

547
00:34:27,893 --> 00:34:29,794
No, it's-

548
00:34:31,099 --> 00:34:33,034
I have no right to be upset.

549
00:34:34,071 --> 00:34:36,233
You two were friends.

550
00:34:39,047 --> 00:34:41,175
You should see her.

551
00:34:41,251 --> 00:34:43,243
Say hi for me.

552
00:34:43,321 --> 00:34:45,415
So, you're okay?

553
00:34:45,492 --> 00:34:49,488
I'm not the cancer doctor
who's lying about the cancer dinner.

554
00:34:50,535 --> 00:34:55,066
I'm not the one betraying
all those poor little bald-headed dying kids.

555
00:34:58,917 --> 00:35:01,547
I'm gonna go get some pants.
I stink.

556
00:35:08,768 --> 00:35:11,534
You're treating him for Addison's
and you don't think it's gonna work?

557
00:35:12,608 --> 00:35:15,340
He tried to kill himself.
I know.

558
00:35:15,413 --> 00:35:19,910
He's confused. We can have another baby.
I can make him understand that.

559
00:35:19,988 --> 00:35:22,389
I'm having an abortion.
We do the transplant-
No.

560
00:35:22,459 --> 00:35:24,485
I can make decisions
about my body.

561
00:35:24,563 --> 00:35:28,900
And he can make decisions about his.
He doesn't want your kidney.

562
00:35:30,407 --> 00:35:33,606
So he'll die?

563
00:35:35,350 --> 00:35:37,342
Probably.

564
00:35:55,519 --> 00:35:59,013
If you keep that appointment,
he'll also probably die.

565
00:36:04,303 --> 00:36:05,999
Keep the baby.

566
00:36:18,996 --> 00:36:20,988
Are you just being polite?

567
00:36:23,905 --> 00:36:25,840
My pants are-

568
00:36:25,908 --> 00:36:28,845
Oh, they're all wet.

569
00:36:32,921 --> 00:36:35,152
You can't smell that?

570
00:36:37,329 --> 00:36:40,528
You think she'll abort anyway,
try to force his hand?

571
00:36:40,602 --> 00:36:43,596
No, she's not gonna
risk losing him.

572
00:36:44,676 --> 00:36:46,645
[Chuckles]
That's funny?

573
00:36:48,182 --> 00:36:52,815
No, the monster trucks.
House asking you, that's- that's funny.

574
00:36:52,891 --> 00:36:56,329
I was the first person he ran into.
He just asked me.

575
00:36:56,398 --> 00:36:58,128
Yeah, like a date.

576
00:36:58,200 --> 00:37:01,399
Exactly.
Except for the date part.

577
00:37:06,883 --> 00:37:11,756
If the patient decides to go the dialysis route,
we've got some product you should check out.

578
00:37:11,825 --> 00:37:14,990
Mmm.
Hey, Dr. Foreman.

579
00:37:15,064 --> 00:37:18,764
Courtesy of the generous Sharon
and the good folks
at Castine Pharmaceuticals.

580
00:37:18,838 --> 00:37:20,966
I was just telling the guys about
the Bermuda conference in April.

581
00:37:21,042 --> 00:37:24,172
Three days of sun and scuba,
and one hour oflecture.

582
00:37:24,247 --> 00:37:26,443
Oh, God, do we have
to go to the lecture?

583
00:37:26,518 --> 00:37:29,489
So, you're the new Arnie.

584
00:37:30,927 --> 00:37:33,123
Dr. House.
It's good to see you.

585
00:37:33,198 --> 00:37:36,533
Would you get me a coffee?
Black, no sugar.

586
00:37:44,418 --> 00:37:46,580
Okay, so who is it?

587
00:37:46,655 --> 00:37:48,681
Come on.
She's sleeping with one of you.

588
00:37:49,560 --> 00:37:52,463
Oh, God, please tell me it's you.

589
00:37:52,533 --> 00:37:54,559
She buys lunches.
She doesn't-

590
00:37:54,636 --> 00:37:56,867
Don't worry. You're not gay.
You're adventurous.

591
00:37:58,076 --> 00:38:01,605
You think she's gonna prostitute herself?
The three of us are that important to her?

592
00:38:01,682 --> 00:38:03,548
I'm afraid not, no.

593
00:38:03,620 --> 00:38:06,785
The groupies sleep with the roadies
in order to get to Mick.

594
00:38:06,859 --> 00:38:10,058
And you're Mick?
That was the metaphor
I was making, yes.

595
00:38:10,131 --> 00:38:13,034
Why are you here?

596
00:38:14,105 --> 00:38:16,131
Damn, it's you.

597
00:38:18,513 --> 00:38:22,418
It's not Addison's.
New symptom. Inability to smell.

598
00:38:22,487 --> 00:38:24,718
I was just in Hank's room.

599
00:38:24,791 --> 00:38:28,229
He said it smelled like the men's room
at Veteran's Stadium. He was right.

600
00:38:28,298 --> 00:38:30,597
We rejected environmental causes
because the wife was healthy.

601
00:38:30,669 --> 00:38:33,663
Well, she's not. Last six months,
she can't smell a thing.

602
00:38:34,810 --> 00:38:39,774
If you think of them as one single patient,
you add her symptoms to his-

603
00:38:39,852 --> 00:38:42,345
Cadmium poisoning.

604
00:38:42,424 --> 00:38:45,759
It explains everything. Even why they
had so much trouble getting pregnant.

605
00:38:45,830 --> 00:38:48,323
How could they have gotten
exposed to that much cadmium?

606
00:38:48,401 --> 00:38:51,304
Unless they were eating
steel and batteries for breakfast.

607
00:38:51,373 --> 00:38:54,708
So, where else is cadmium?
Some foods,
polluted groundwater.

608
00:38:54,779 --> 00:38:57,773
We should check their home.
I think I know
how it happened.

609
00:38:59,955 --> 00:39:01,787
I'm gonna need
another urine sample.

610
00:39:01,859 --> 00:39:04,021
What for?
Sure.

611
00:39:04,097 --> 00:39:05,531
[Hank]
Whatever you want.

612
00:39:05,599 --> 00:39:08,297
Why wouldn't you give it to me before,
but now it's no problem?

613
00:39:08,371 --> 00:39:12,208
- I'm dyin', right?
- So you've got nothing to lose this time.

614
00:39:13,580 --> 00:39:17,018
Begs the question,
what were you worried about last time?

615
00:39:18,222 --> 00:39:22,059
The funny thing is,
when we tested you before,
we were just looking for steroids.

616
00:39:22,129 --> 00:39:25,157
What should we look for now, Hank?

617
00:39:25,235 --> 00:39:29,174
Hank, what's the story?

618
00:39:30,110 --> 00:39:33,343
A little weed every now and then
when no one was looking?

619
00:39:37,590 --> 00:39:39,821
I don't believe this.

620
00:39:39,895 --> 00:39:42,194
- We quit.
- You did.

621
00:39:42,266 --> 00:39:44,998
If you'd kept going, you wouldn't
have just lost your sense of smell.

622
00:39:45,071 --> 00:39:46,539
I quit the hard stuff.

623
00:39:48,343 --> 00:39:52,476
- I just needed to relax.
- Based on the symptoms,
you're a lot more than a social user.

624
00:39:52,551 --> 00:39:56,388
So you've been lying to me
all this time?
I'm sorry.

625
00:39:56,459 --> 00:39:59,919
There must have been
cadmium in the soil
where the marijuana was grown.

626
00:39:59,998 --> 00:40:05,269
Some people get bone loss,
kidney failure,
some people's testes shrink,

627
00:40:05,341 --> 00:40:08,801
and some people
lose their sense of smell.

628
00:40:08,881 --> 00:40:10,679
We'll start treatment
right away.

629
00:40:10,751 --> 00:40:13,483
You should be fine by opening day.

630
00:40:13,556 --> 00:40:15,923
Baseball's in the summer, right?

631
00:40:15,994 --> 00:40:18,156
It didn't hurt the baby, did it?
The cadmium?

632
00:40:18,232 --> 00:40:22,137
- If you've been clean,
the baby should be fine.
- Okay.

633
00:40:24,409 --> 00:40:29,179
Please. I'll stop everything.
I'll- I'll go to meetings every day.

634
00:40:32,290 --> 00:40:34,691
Lola.

635
00:40:36,565 --> 00:40:38,557
Twice a day.

636
00:40:40,004 --> 00:40:41,768
How's the ballplayer doing?

637
00:40:41,841 --> 00:40:44,539
Much better.
Too bad about his career.

638
00:40:44,612 --> 00:40:45,944
What do you mean?

639
00:40:46,015 --> 00:40:48,041
Major League Baseball's
collective bargaining agreement...

640
00:40:48,119 --> 00:40:50,612
requires medical reports
on all treatment.

641
00:40:50,690 --> 00:40:53,286
Given Hank's history,
he's not likely to get much leniency.

642
00:40:53,361 --> 00:40:56,298
Why should they care
that he's being treated for Addison's?

643
00:40:56,367 --> 00:40:59,236
You're not treating him
for Addison's.
My report says I am.

644
00:40:59,306 --> 00:41:01,332
You're lying on the report?

645
00:41:02,412 --> 00:41:04,347
Well, everybody does stupid things.

646
00:41:04,416 --> 00:41:06,852
It shouldn't cost them
everything they want in life.

647
00:41:07,921 --> 00:41:11,381
No, it shouldn't,
but it usually does.

648
00:41:11,461 --> 00:41:15,696
On the other hand,
if it means someone
can actually beat the Yankees-

649
00:41:19,209 --> 00:41:22,203
So what about House?
Is there any way
we can get him down there?

650
00:41:25,454 --> 00:41:28,254
You really wanna talk
about work?

651
00:41:29,794 --> 00:41:32,356
No. Not at all.

652
00:41:48,863 --> 00:41:52,357
[Engines Rewing]
[Spectators Cheering,
Applauding]

653
00:41:53,972 --> 00:41:55,873
That was amazing!

654
00:41:55,943 --> 00:41:59,244
I'm telling you.
Grave Digger never disappoints.

655
00:42:04,992 --> 00:42:06,984
You ever been married?

656
00:42:08,498 --> 00:42:11,992
Well, now, let's not ruin
a lovely night out
by getting personal.

657
00:42:14,009 --> 00:42:16,502
I lived with someone
for a while.

658
00:42:18,416 --> 00:42:20,408
You gonna finish that?

659
00:42:23,893 --> 00:42:26,921
[Mumbling]
[Laughs]

660
00:42:27,000 --> 00:42:29,026
[Cameron]
I'll race you to the car.

661
00:43:05,369 --> 00:43:06,632
That's some bad hat, Harry.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
